Power materials, loss, environment and recovery (@pe-environment: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Improving-Motor-and-Drive-System-Performance-DOE.lingua#r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR", #source "../sources/Motor-Rewind-Study-and-Good-Practice-EASA-AEMT.lingua#r_3K38XSH8DWC79G20NF55ATKEJP", #source "../sources/Medium-Voltage-Technical-Guide-Schneider.lingua#r_77NSGJV2R4FM4513WTNWE456J2", #electrical-power-engineering "Electrical-service-from-materials-to-modern-production.lingua#r_0J3CKGT5DZ697CY2X114MY4WSN") { r_0VYYF0CTRSVGX2CGC7Z9ZPSTHA
**Read:** [Improving Motor and Drive System Performance — DOE](../sources/Improving-Motor-and-Drive-System-Performance-DOE.lingua#r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR), whole useful-system, repair/selection and life-cycle discussion; [Motor rewind studies and good practice — EASA/AEMT](../sources/Motor-Rewind-Study-and-Good-Practice-EASA-AEMT.lingua#r_3K38XSH8DWC79G20NF55ATKEJP), both entire studies and their actual limits; [Medium Voltage Technical Guide — Schneider Electric](../sources/Medium-Voltage-Technical-Guide-Schneider.lingua#r_77NSGJV2R4FM4513WTNWE456J2), complete applicable environmental and material/service context.

Electrical service uses copper/aluminium, electrical steels, magnets, insulation, semiconductors, oils/fluids, structural materials and energy-supply systems. Their production, condition, loss, replacement and recovery have physical consequences beyond a terminal efficiency number. Connect composition/processing and material measurements to actual electrical and thermal capability.

For one transformer, motor, converter or feeder, trace useful service, losses, lifetime assumptions, maintenance material, repair/replacement and end-of-life flows. Compare two designs on the same duty and boundary. A lower purchase cost, lower running loss and lower total resource/environment burden are different claims requiring different evidence.

Use [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../../../../ergon/materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1), [Industrial chemistry — chemical transformations, useful products and continuing production](../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/Industrial-chemistry.lingua#r_3AKBAFB2ABJ0671QW6ZBQ0B618) and [Resources and materials — feedstocks, useful properties, production, and recovery](../../../../ergon/materials/Materials.lingua#r_14HP6K610XB12E2WGNK9A6VN8D) for the already developed production/material foundations, with ordinary references to deeper specialist subjects as they become available. Keep hazardous/regulated material handling and actual current requirements attached to the chosen physical case rather than prescribing a generic disposal method. The full [Motor rewind studies and good practice — EASA/AEMT](../sources/Motor-Rewind-Study-and-Good-Practice-EASA-AEMT.lingua#r_3K38XSH8DWC79G20NF55ATKEJP) and [Improving Motor and Drive System Performance — DOE](../sources/Improving-Motor-and-Drive-System-Performance-DOE.lingua#r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR) readings demonstrate why maintaining an efficient device can be a material/technical decision as well as an energy calculation.

